3. ZERO-DEPENDENCY CLEAN-ROOM STANDARD LIBRARY ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Logihertz Systems open-source ecosystem is engineered under a strict, non-negotiable
clean-room standard library invariant across all 60 standalone repositories:

- Python Engines (35 Repositories): Strictly Python 3.11+ standard library.
- Rust Engines (5 Repositories): Pure Rust 2021 with `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`.
- Go Engines (5 Repositories): Pure Go 1.22+ standard library (`go.mod` zero `require`).
- C11 Engines (5 Repositories): Pure ISO C11 (`-std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror`).
- C++17 Engines (4 Repositories): Pure ISO C++17 with AVX2 & ARM NEON vectorization.
- PHP Engines (3 Repositories): Pure PHP 8.2+ core & standard extensions (`ext-hash`, `ext-json`).
- TypeScript Engines (2 Repositories): Strict ES2022 TypeScript without npm dependencies.
- SELinux Policy (1 Repository): Pure SELinux Common Intermediate Language (CIL).

Every binary and library operates 100% offline in air-gapped mission-critical environments
with zero transitive supply-chain attack surface.

